// P6: correlated-variable precision loss (non-relational domain).
// y = x on every concrete run, hence d = x - y + 1 is ALWAYS 1 and the
// division never sees a zero divisor.  The interval analysis, however,
// evaluates each variable independently as [-1,1]:
//
//     [-1,1] - [-1,1] + 1 = [-1, 3]
//
// which contains 0, so it warns about a possible division by zero that can
// never happen.  This is a documented false positive and marks the boundary
// of the non-relational interval domain (a relational/trace domain would
// keep the correlation y = x).
input x;
var y = 0;
var q = 0;
y = x;
q = 5 / (x - y + 1);
